   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Ben Pennell",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "While objects like this can be difficult to deal with, it does seem that if you perform a MOVE directly against indexed pair tree nodes you can rename them to something without the index, and then interact with the path. For example:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "attrs": {
         "language": "java"
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "curl -X MOVE -H \"Destination: http://localhost:8181/fcrepo/rest/deposits/a9_2\" \"http://localhost:8181/fcrepo/rest/deposits/a9%5B2%5D\"",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "codeBlock"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Succeeds but sometimes returns the message \"There is no node that will serve as the parent of the moved item\". You can then move anything contained within that path to the correct path. If WebAC is enabled, then it may require encoding the characters here (this breaks some tests):",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/fcrepo-5.1.0/fcrepo-auth-webac/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/auth/webac/WebACFilter.java#L190"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/fcrepo-5.1.0/fcrepo-auth-webac/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/auth/webac/WebACFilter.java#L190",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "attrs": {
         "language": "java"
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "String requestUrl = httpRequest.getRequestURL().toString();\r\nrequestUrl = requestUrl.replace(\"[\", \"%5B\").replace(\"]\", \"%5D\");",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "codeBlock"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "As otherwise URI.create will fail on unencoded []s.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
