  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Multiple requests attempting to create new objects in pairtrees where pairtree components share the same name can result in generating invalid pairtree names. For example, the following operations can produce the issue:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "java"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "PUT http://localhost:8080/fcrepo/rest/base\r\nstart tx:1\r\n\r\nPUT http://localhost:8080/fcrepo/rest/tx:1/base/path/to/myobj1\r\n\r\nstart tx:2\r\n\r\nPUT http://localhost:8080/fcrepo/rest/tx:2/base/path/to/myobj2\r\n\r\ncommit tx:1 and tx:2",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If the two commits are concurrent, then the result can be the following resources being created:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "java"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "http://localhost:8080/fcrepo/rest/base/path/to/myobj1\r\n\r\nhttp://localhost:8080/fcrepo/rest/base/path[2]/to/myobj2",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The issue can be reproduced with the following integration test:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://gist.github.com/bbpennel/c5684c114586c257e57e54bbfcb0ee0b"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://gist.github.com/bbpennel/c5684c114586c257e57e54bbfcb0ee0b",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Attempting to perform modification operations on either myobj1 or myobj2 will produce variations on the following error (exact stacktrace depends on the operation):",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "java"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "curl -XPUT http://localhost:8080/d61a4b67-fe3d-4807-b03a-cc121234b877/path/to/obj2/child\r\n\r\njavax.jcr.nodetype.ConstraintViolationException: Cannot find a definition for a child named '{}path' on the node at '/d61a4b67-fe3d-4807-b03a-cc121234b877' with primary type 'nt:folder' and mixin types: [fedora:Container,fedora:Resource,ldp:BasicContainer]\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.nodeDefinition(AbstractJcrNode.java:2913)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.getDefinition(AbstractJcrNode.java:2837)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.isCheckedOut(AbstractJcrNode.java:3220)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addChildNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:1133)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:1074)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:988)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:102)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.api.JcrTools.findOrCreateNode(JcrTools.java:437)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.api.JcrTools.findOrCreateNode(JcrTools.java:377)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.modeshape.services.AbstractService.findOrCreateNode(AbstractService.java:67)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.modeshape.services.ContainerServiceImpl.findOrCreate(ContainerServiceImpl.java:78)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.http.api.FedoraLdp.createFedoraResource(FedoraLdp.java:802)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.http.api.FedoraLdp.createOrReplaceObjectRdf(FedoraLdp.java:438)\r\n...",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "You can produce similar outcomes with DELETE and MOVE operations, probably POST as well. Performing a GET directly against \"path[2]\" will throw an error if WebAC is turned on, due to an encoding issue with the brackets.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Note: the basic container \"base\" (or \"d61a4b67-fe3d-4807-b03a-cc121234b877\" in the example above) was not necessary to produce the sibling count indexed pair trees. However, if I placed the pair tree at the root of the repository, no exceptions were thrown when performing operations on objects in the pair tree.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is the same issue as ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-2086"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-2086",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " where the resolution explicitly does not cover transactions.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
