      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0f212807d7bbe91a49a7c4620c5bfdac?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBP-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Ben Pennell",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>While objects like this can be difficult to deal with, it does seem that if you perform a MOVE directly against indexed pair tree nodes you can rename them to something without the index, and then interact with the path. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\ncurl -X MOVE -H <span class=\"code-quote\">\"Destination: http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8181/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/deposits/a9_2\"</span> <span class=\"code-quote\">\"http://localhost:8181/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/deposits/a9%5B2%5D\"</span></span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>Succeeds but sometimes returns the message \"There is no node that will serve as the parent of the moved item\". You can then move anything contained within that path to the correct path. If WebAC is enabled, then it may require encoding the characters here (this breaks some tests):</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/fcrepo-5.1.0/fcrepo-auth-webac/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/auth/webac/WebACFilter.java#L190\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/fcrepo-5.1.0/fcrepo-auth-webac/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/auth/webac/WebACFilter.java#L190</a></p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n<span class=\"code-object\">String</span> requestUrl = httpRequest.getRequestURL().toString();\r\nrequestUrl = requestUrl.replace(<span class=\"code-quote\">\"[\"</span>, <span class=\"code-quote\">\"%5B\"</span>).replace(<span class=\"code-quote\">\"]\"</span>, <span class=\"code-quote\">\"%5D\"</span>);\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>As otherwise URI.create will fail on unencoded []s.</p>",
     "created": "26/Jun/20 7:27 PM",
