  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>Multiple requests attempting to create new objects in pairtrees where pairtree components share the same name can result in generating invalid pairtree names. For example, the following operations can produce the issue:</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\nPUT http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/base\r\n</span>start tx:1\r\n\r\nPUT http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/tx:1/base/path/to/myobj1\r\n</span>\r\nstart tx:2\r\n\r\nPUT http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/tx:2/base/path/to/myobj2\r\n</span>\r\ncommit tx:1 and tx:2\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>If the two commits are concurrent, then the result can be the following resources being created:</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\nhttp:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/base/path/to/myobj1\r\n</span>\r\nhttp:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/fcrepo/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/base/path[2]/to/myobj2</span>\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>The issue can be reproduced with the following integration test:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://gist.github.com/bbpennel/c5684c114586c257e57e54bbfcb0ee0b\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://gist.github.com/bbpennel/c5684c114586c257e57e54bbfcb0ee0b</a></p>\n\n<p>Attempting to perform modification operations on either myobj1 or myobj2 will produce variations on the following error (exact stacktrace depends on the operation):</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\ncurl -XPUT http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/d61a4b67-fe3d-4807-b03a-cc121234b877/path/to/obj2/child\r\n</span>\r\njavax.jcr.nodetype.ConstraintViolationException: Cannot find a definition <span class=\"code-keyword\">for</span> a child named <span class=\"code-quote\">'{}path'</span> on the node at <span class=\"code-quote\">'/d61a4b67-fe3d-4807-b03a-cc121234b877'</span> with primary type <span class=\"code-quote\">'nt:folder'</span> and mixin types: [fedora:Container,fedora:Resource,ldp:BasicContainer]\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.nodeDefinition(AbstractJcrNode.java:2913)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.getDefinition(AbstractJcrNode.java:2837)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.isCheckedOut(AbstractJcrNode.java:3220)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addChildNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:1133)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:1074)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:988)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.AbstractJcrNode.addNode(AbstractJcrNode.java:102)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.api.JcrTools.findOrCreateNode(JcrTools.java:437)\r\n\tat org.modeshape.jcr.api.JcrTools.findOrCreateNode(JcrTools.java:377)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.modeshape.services.AbstractService.findOrCreateNode(AbstractService.java:67)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.modeshape.services.ContainerServiceImpl.findOrCreate(ContainerServiceImpl.java:78)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.http.api.FedoraLdp.createFedoraResource(FedoraLdp.java:802)\r\n\tat org.fcrepo.http.api.FedoraLdp.createOrReplaceObjectRdf(FedoraLdp.java:438)\r\n...\r\n\r\n</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>You can produce similar outcomes with DELETE and MOVE operations, probably POST as well. Performing a GET directly against \"path<span class=\"error\">&#91;2&#93;</span>\" will throw an error if WebAC is turned on, due to an encoding issue with the brackets.</p>\n\n<p>Note: the basic container \"base\" (or \"d61a4b67-fe3d-4807-b03a-cc121234b877\" in the example above) was not necessary to produce the sibling count indexed pair trees. However, if I placed the pair tree at the root of the repository, no exceptions were thrown when performing operations on objects in the pair tree.</p>\n\n<p>This is the same issue as <a href=\"https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-2086\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/FCREPO-2086</a> where the resolution explicitly does not cover transactions.</p>",
